The most cpu the objects of this namespace may be capped to, cluster-wide, in
the pg_cpu_quota notation: 800% or 100%@8 is eight cpus.

An object claims what its processes are capped to, on every instance it may
run at once: one for a failover object, its flex_target for a flex one, plus
the standby resources of the other instances. A configuration write taking
the namespace over the limit is refused, and so is a process capped by
nothing, which takes what it finds: give the containers a default with the
default keyword of this claim.

The cpus of a node are not a quantity of the cluster, so @all is refused.
